[
    {
        "id": "368d9e12-2ade-4277-bf8a-e2cb15e6c94e",
        "father_name": "Theodoret of Cyrus",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_23.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 458,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000023,
        "location_end": 17000023,
        "txt": "He says, know that it is easy for me both to humble what is lofty and to raise up what is lowly; to make dry what is wet and to manifest what is dry to be in flower.\n",
        "source_url": "",
        "source_title": "COMMENTARY ON EZEKIEL 6"
    },
    {
        "id": "a10af5b4-9a2c-4165-9d9f-e310243d53c7",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_3.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000003,
        "location_end": 17000003,
        "txt": "He came to that Lebanon, which is the church, where the offerings of God and the incense of his prayers are celebrated, that great true evil, Nebuchadnezzar, that is, the devil, and he sees it.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 11:5"
    },
    {
        "id": "67c40a83-1811-4f64-b72a-4aeadde3c6d1",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_6.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000006,
        "location_end": 17000006,
        "txt": "As long as it was on holy ground, the vine was huge; but when it was taken to the land of sinners, it was made infirm and small.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 11:4"
    },
    {
        "id": "492093b1-32fa-4203-b325-8d5e9126b679",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_12.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000012,
        "location_end": 17000012,
        "txt": "I am inclined to think that by the good quality of their conduct they increase yet more the agreeableness of the words of God, mixing the sweetness of the life with the sweet savor of the word.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:1"
    },
    {
        "id": "a4843228-38ad-481d-9570-d78375ad327c",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_12.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000012,
        "location_end": 17000012,
        "txt": "If we who appear to stand over the church have sinned and given place to the devil against the teaching of Paul when he says \u201cdo not give any place to the devil,\u201d in the same way the faults committed at Jerusalem mean that we provide Nebuchadnezzar with the chance to enter into the holy city and to take away those whom he chooses.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:2"
    },
    {
        "id": "e12cfa10-d8bf-49b4-aaf6-1b31da470e69",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_23.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000023,
        "location_end": 17000023,
        "txt": "Consider the sublime grandeur of the church of Christ, to understand that according to the promise of God the word has been realized.\u2026 It will become a noble cedar; and under it will dwell all kinds of beasts; in the shade of its branches birds of every sort will nest.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:5"
    },
    {
        "id": "2199c98b-2d3f-4b17-88b6-0b26ce7c347a",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_23.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000023,
        "location_end": 17000023,
        "txt": "Take the wings of the word of God, and you will be able to repose under this tree that has been planted over a high mountain.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:5"
    },
    {
        "id": "093fb7de-3a5f-416a-91ca-dbf7f9242a2d",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_13.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000013,
        "location_end": 17000013,
        "txt": "If you have the covenant with us in a blessing, Nebuchadnezzar cannot make a covenant with you.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:3"
    },
    {
        "id": "031e93a0-c6a9-46de-aeae-972e8972e231",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_13.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000013,
        "location_end": 17000013,
        "txt": "God makes covenant with us in a blessing; Nebuchadnezzar establishes his covenant in abuse.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:3"
    },
    {
        "id": "b6e193c2-aeb7-4759-9e1c-bae073a90fb1",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_22.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000022,
        "location_end": 17000022,
        "txt": "There is one who dishonors the judgment of God; there is another who honors it.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:4"
    },
    {
        "id": "c6a2eba4-91b1-493a-b1ba-a99364f7f579",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_22.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000022,
        "location_end": 17000022,
        "txt": "To the one who has transgressed and has dishonored the judgment of God, Pharaoh cannot come to the rescue; he will die in the center of Babylon for his transgressions.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:4"
    },
    {
        "id": "b0955691-7da6-49b6-b975-6f4326cc24fa",
        "father_name": "Origen of Alexandria",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_16.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 253,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000016,
        "location_end": 17000016,
        "txt": "As holy Scripture tells us, God intends that the covenant with Israel is an abuse against Nebuchadnezzar.\n",
        "source_url": "https://historicalchristian.faith/by_father.php?file=Origen%2520of%2520Alexandria%2FHomilies%2520on%2520Ezekiel%2FTranslation-Hooker-Pearse.pdf",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES ON EZEKIEL 12:3"
    },
    {
        "id": "4dd4eb34-515f-4d2e-9fbf-4c2f1cf44313",
        "father_name": "John Chrysostom",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_6.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 407,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000006,
        "location_end": 17000006,
        "txt": "[Ezekiel] calls the city of Jerusalem a vine; but in saying that it stretched out its branches towards the eagle and that its roots were under him, he refers to the treaties and alliances made with him and that it cast itself on him.\n",
        "source_url": "",
        "source_title": "HOMILIES CONCERNING THE STATUES 19:9"
    },
    {
        "id": "42634052-87ee-487e-a893-22b0150a4bc7",
        "father_name": "Jerome",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_6.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 420,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000006,
        "location_end": 17000006,
        "txt": "Whoever has been under the wings of this sun [of justice and healing] who has said in the Gospel: how often would I have gathered your children together, as a hen gathers her young under her wings, but you would not! shall be safe from the devil hawk, safe under the great wings of that mighty eagle in Ezekiel, and all the wounds of his sins shall be healed.\n",
        "source_url": "",
        "source_title": "HOMILY 94 (ON EASTER SUNDAY)"
    },
    {
        "id": "73dfce49-11eb-4bda-a3f4-0df598d55731",
        "father_name": "Jerome",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_23.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 420,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000023,
        "location_end": 17000023,
        "txt": "The high tree humbled and the humble tree exalted refer to the passion of the Lord and Savior, \u201cwho, though he was in the form of God, did not count equality with God a theme to be grasped, but he emptied himself, taking the form of a servant,\u201d and after the resurrection, this very wood was afterwards raised high, which was fair and strong, and then made dry in death, and after reviving, received back its original strength.\n",
        "source_url": "",
        "source_title": "COMMENTARY ON EZEKIEL 5:17.22-24"
    },
    {
        "id": "8a9ce323-5c1f-4a05-b097-42beb0115482",
        "father_name": "Jerome",
        "file_name": "Ezekiel 17_1.toml",
        "append_to_author_name": "",
        "ts": 420,
        "book": "ezekiel",
        "location_start": 17000001,
        "location_end": 17000001,
        "txt": "To no one is there any doubt that the prophet makes known one thing in words as an allegory and a parable but means something else, for even the Savior spoke to the people in parables, which he explained in secret to the apostles. Therefore we must understand the allegory and the parable for what they are. There are two eagles that are placed before us in this part of the prophecy of Ezekiel.\n",
        "source_url": "",
        "source_title": "COMMENTARY ON EZEKIEL 5:17.1-6"
    }
]